-- Canada Pension Plan Act, Part I, Division B -- sections 13, 14 and 14.1: CONTRIBUTORY SELF-EMPLOYED EARNINGS and
-- SELF-EMPLOYED EARNINGS.
--
-- The self-employed earnings of a person for a year (section 14) are the income from businesses, plus some employment
-- income excepted by regulation, plus some Indian income on a reserve. The contributory self-employed earnings
-- (section 13) are those earnings, prorated by months in the year of reaching eighteen or seventy, of the end of the
-- contributory period, of the disability pension ceasing, and of the elections of subparagraph 12(1)(c)(ii) and
-- paragraphs 13(1)(b) and (c); with the exclusions of subsection 13(2) and the elections of subsections 13(3) to (3.2).
--
-- Months are counted by cp1-months-helpers.l4. Ages go through the keel's section 2(2) rules: paragraphs 13(1)(c) and (e)
-- and 13(1.2)(c) are among the ten places where the actual birthday governs (the constructors
-- `paragraph 13(1)(c)`, `paragraph 13(1)(e)` and `paragraph 13(1.2)(c)`); paragraphs 13(1)(a), (b) and (d) and 13(1.2)(a)
-- are not (`any other provision`).
--
-- out of range: the Income Tax Act is not part of this text: the income and losses "computed under" it are plain inputs.
-- out of range: the Indian Act is not part of this text: "Indian" and "reserve".
-- out of range: regulation 84.1 (piece cr1): the extent of an Indian's income from self-employment on a reserve for paragraph 14(c).
-- out of range: regulation 2(2) (piece cr1) and regulations made under subsection 7(1) (Part III of the Regulations, piece cr1): services included in pensionable employment.
-- out of range: section 49 (piece cp3): the contributory period and the excluded months.
-- out of range: section 44 (piece cp3) and section 67 (piece cp5): "a retirement pension is payable".
-- out of range: regulations 83.2 and 84 (piece cr1): the form and manner of the elections of subsections 13(1.1) and 13(3).
-- out of range: section 38 (piece cp2): the Minister's refund to an employee, in subsection 13(3).
-- out of range: regulation 6.1 (piece cr1): the salary and wages on which a provincial contribution was made, "determined in the prescribed manner".
-- The amounts of sections 15, 17, 17.1 and 19 are the sibling modules'; the caller passes their results.

§ `Division B -- Calculation of Contributions`

§§ `Section 14 -- the amount of self-employed earnings for a year`

-- src:431 | Amount of self-employed earnings for a year
-- src:432 | 14 The amount of the self-employed earnings of a person for a year is the aggregate of
-- src:433 | (a) an amount equal to
-- src:434 | (i) his income for the year from all businesses, other than a business more than fifty per cent of the gross revenue of which consisted of rent from land or buildings, carried on by him,
-- src:435 | minus
-- src:436 | (ii) all losses sustained by him in the year in carrying on those businesses,
-- src:437 | as such income and losses are computed under the Income Tax Act, except any such income or losses from the performance of services described in paragraph 7(1)(d) that has been included in pensionable employment by a regulation made under subsection 7(1) or by a regulation made under a provincial pension plan,
-- src:438 | (b) his income for the year from employment described in paragraph 7(2)(e) that has been excepted from pensionable employment by a regulation made under subsection 7(2) or by a regulation made under a provincial pension plan, as that income is computed under the Income Tax Act, and
-- src:439 | (c) in the case of an Indian, as defined in the Indian Act, to the extent provided by regulations and subject to any conditions prescribed by those regulations, his income for the year from self-employment on a reserve, as defined in the Indian Act, that is not otherwise included in computing income for the purposes of the Income Tax Act.
@ref Act s 14(a) (src:433-437)
GIVEN businesses IS A LIST OF `cp1 Business carried on by a person`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 14(a) — the income from businesses, less the losses sustained in carrying them on` businesses MEANS
        sum (map (GIVEN business YIELD business's `income of the person for the year from the business`) `the businesses counted`)
    MINUS sum (map (GIVEN business YIELD business's `losses sustained by the person in the year in carrying on the business`) `the businesses counted`)
    WHERE
        -- "all businesses, other than a business more than fifty per cent of the gross revenue of which consisted of rent from land or buildings",
        -- "except any such income or losses from the performance of services described in paragraph 7(1)(d) that has been included in pensionable employment by a regulation"
        `the business is counted` business MEANS
                (NOT business's `more than fifty per cent of the gross revenue of the business consisted of rent from land or buildings`)
            AND (NOT business's `the income or losses are from services described in paragraph 7(1)(d) that a regulation has included in pensionable employment`)
        `the businesses counted` MEANS filter `the business is counted` businesses

@ref Act s 14(b) (src:438)
GIVEN `the person's income for the year from employment described in paragraph 7(2)(e) that has been excepted from pensionable employment, as computed under the Income Tax Act` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 14(b) — the income from employment described in paragraph 7(2)(e) that has been excepted from pensionable employment` `the person's income for the year from employment described in paragraph 7(2)(e) that has been excepted from pensionable employment, as computed under the Income Tax Act` MEANS
    `the person's income for the year from employment described in paragraph 7(2)(e) that has been excepted from pensionable employment, as computed under the Income Tax Act`

@ref Act s 14(c) (src:439)
GIVEN `the person is an Indian as defined in the Indian Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the income for the year from self-employment on a reserve that is not otherwise included in computing income for the purposes of the Income Tax Act, to the extent provided by regulations and subject to any conditions prescribed by them` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 14(c) — the income of an Indian from self-employment on a reserve` `the person is an Indian as defined in the Indian Act` `the income for the year from self-employment on a reserve that is not otherwise included in computing income for the purposes of the Income Tax Act, to the extent provided by regulations and subject to any conditions prescribed by them` MEANS
    IF `the person is an Indian as defined in the Indian Act`
    THEN JUST `the income for the year from self-employment on a reserve that is not otherwise included in computing income for the purposes of the Income Tax Act, to the extent provided by regulations and subject to any conditions prescribed by them`
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref Act s 14 (src:431-439)
GIVEN paragraph14a IS A NUMBER
      paragraph14b IS A NUMBER
      paragraph14c IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 14 — the self-employed earnings of a person for a year` paragraph14a paragraph14b paragraph14c MEANS
    paragraph14a PLUS paragraph14b PLUS fromMaybe 0 paragraph14c

-- src:440 | Idem
-- src:441 | 14.1 For the purposes of paragraph 14(a), where a member of a family in a congregation is specified in an election under subsection 143(2) of the Income Tax Act for a year, such part of the total of all amounts allocated to the family under that subsection for the year as may reasonably be regarded as having been derived from a business carried on by the congregation shall be deemed to be the member’s income (as computed under that Act) from such a business carried on by the member.
@ref Act s 14.1 (src:440-441)
GIVEN `a member of a family in a congregation is specified in an election under subsection 143(2) of the Income Tax Act for the year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the part of the total of all amounts allocated to the family under that subsection for the year that may reasonably be regarded as having been derived from a business carried on by the congregation` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 14.1 — the income deemed to be the member's income from a business carried on by the member` `a member of a family in a congregation is specified in an election under subsection 143(2) of the Income Tax Act for the year` `the part of the total of all amounts allocated to the family under that subsection for the year that may reasonably be regarded as having been derived from a business carried on by the congregation` MEANS
    IF `a member of a family in a congregation is specified in an election under subsection 143(2) of the Income Tax Act for the year`
    THEN JUST `the part of the total of all amounts allocated to the family under that subsection for the year that may reasonably be regarded as having been derived from a business carried on by the congregation`
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Section 13(1.1) and (1.2) -- the elections to exclude self-employed earnings`

-- src:375 | Election
-- src:376 | (1.1) An election referred to in paragraph (1)(b) or (c)
-- src:377 | (a) shall be made or revoked in the prescribed form and manner;
-- src:378 | (b) may be made only once for a year;
-- src:379 | (c) may not be revoked for the year for which it is deemed to be made;
-- src:380 | (d) may not be made for a year for which an election is revoked;
-- src:381 | (e) is deemed to be made or revoked on the first day of the month referred to in the election or revocation, as the case may be; and
-- src:382 | (f) may not be made for a year for which the person has income from pensionable employment.
-- src:383 | Condition
-- src:384 | (1.2) For the purposes of paragraph (1.1)(e), the month may not be
-- src:385 | (a) before the one in which the person reaches sixty-five years of age;
-- src:386 | (b) before the one in which the retirement pension becomes payable; or
-- src:387 | (c) after the one in which they reach seventy years of age.
@ref Act s 13(1.1)(a) (src:377)
GIVEN `the election is made or revoked in the prescribed form and manner` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 13(1.1)(a) — the election or the revocation is valid in form` `the election is made or revoked in the prescribed form and manner` MEANS
    `the election is made or revoked in the prescribed form and manner`

@ref Act s 13(1.1)(b) (src:378)
GIVEN `an election has already been made for the year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 13(1.1)(b) — the election may be made for the year` `an election has already been made for the year` MEANS
    NOT `an election has already been made for the year`

@ref Act s 13(1.1)(c) (src:379)
GIVEN `year for which the election is deemed to be made` IS A NUMBER
      `year for which the election is revoked` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 13(1.1)(c) — the election may be revoked for the year` `year for which the election is deemed to be made` `year for which the election is revoked` MEANS
    NOT (`year for which the election is revoked` EQUALS `year for which the election is deemed to be made`)

@ref Act s 13(1.1)(d) (src:380)
GIVEN `an election is revoked for the year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 13(1.1)(d) — the election may be made for the year` `an election is revoked for the year` MEANS
    NOT `an election is revoked for the year`

@ref Act s 13(1.1)(e) (src:381)
GIVEN `month referred to in the election or revocation` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 13(1.1)(e) — the day on which the election is deemed to be made or revoked` `month referred to in the election or revocation` MEANS
    `the month of a date` `month referred to in the election or revocation`

-- Whether an election under paragraph 13(1)(b) has effect in a month: from the first day of the month referred to in the election
-- (it is deemed made on that day) until the day before the first day of the month referred to in a revocation (deemed made on that day).
@ref Act s 13(1.1)(e) (src:381)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      `month referred to in the election` IS A MAYBE DATE
      `month referred to in the revocation` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 13(1.1) — an election under paragraph 13(1)(b) has effect in a month` month `month referred to in the election` `month referred to in the revocation` MEANS
    CONSIDER `month referred to in the election`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST made THEN
            `the month of a date` month AT LEAST `s 13(1.1)(e) — the day on which the election is deemed to be made or revoked` made
        AND (CONSIDER `month referred to in the revocation`
             WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
             WHEN JUST revoked THEN `the month of a date` month LESS THAN `s 13(1.1)(e) — the day on which the election is deemed to be made or revoked` revoked)

@ref Act s 13(1.1)(f) (src:382)
GIVEN `the person has income from pensionable employment for the year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 13(1.1)(f) — the election may be made for the year in view of income from pensionable employment` `the person has income from pensionable employment for the year` MEANS
    NOT `the person has income from pensionable employment for the year`

-- An election may be made for a year only if it is in the prescribed form and manner (a), none has been made for the
-- year (b), none is revoked for it (d), and the person has no income from pensionable employment for it (f).
@ref Act s 13(1.1) (src:376-382)
GIVEN `the election is made or revoked in the prescribed form and manner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an election has already been made for the year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an election is revoked for the year` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has income from pensionable employment for the year` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 13(1.1) — a valid election under paragraph 13(1)(b) may be made for the year` `the election is made or revoked in the prescribed form and manner` `an election has already been made for the year` `an election is revoked for the year` `the person has income from pensionable employment for the year` MEANS
        `s 13(1.1)(a) — the election or the revocation is valid in form` `the election is made or revoked in the prescribed form and manner`
    AND `s 13(1.1)(b) — the election may be made for the year` `an election has already been made for the year`
    AND `s 13(1.1)(d) — the election may be made for the year` `an election is revoked for the year`
    AND `s 13(1.1)(f) — the election may be made for the year in view of income from pensionable employment` `the person has income from pensionable employment for the year`

-- The month an election refers to may not be (a) before the one in which the person reaches sixty-five, (b) before the
-- one in which the retirement pension becomes payable, or (c) after the one in which they reach seventy. Paragraph (c) is
-- one of the ten places where the actual birthday governs.
@ref Act s 13(1.2)(a) (src:385)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      `date of birth` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 13(1.2)(a) — the month is not before the month in which the person reaches sixty-five years of age` month `date of birth` MEANS
    `the month of a date` month AT LEAST `the month of a date` (`s 2(2) — the date a person is treated as reaching a specified age for a provision` `any other provision` `date of birth` 65)

@ref Act s 13(1.2)(b) (src:386)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      `month in which the retirement pension becomes payable` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 13(1.2)(b) — the month is not before the month in which the retirement pension becomes payable` month `month in which the retirement pension becomes payable` MEANS
    `the month of a date` month AT LEAST `the month of a date` `month in which the retirement pension becomes payable`

@ref Act s 13(1.2)(c) (src:387)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      `date of birth` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 13(1.2)(c) — the month is not after the month in which the person reaches seventy years of age` month `date of birth` MEANS
    `the month of a date` month AT MOST `the month of a date` (`s 2(2) — the date a person is treated as reaching a specified age for a provision` `paragraph 13(1.2)(c)` `date of birth` 70)

@ref Act s 13(1.2) (src:383-387)
GIVEN month IS A DATE
      `date of birth` IS A DATE
      `month in which the retirement pension becomes payable` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 13(1.2) — the month referred to in the election or revocation is allowed` month `date of birth` `month in which the retirement pension becomes payable` MEANS
        `s 13(1.2)(a) — the month is not before the month in which the person reaches sixty-five years of age` month `date of birth`
    AND `s 13(1.2)(b) — the month is not before the month in which the retirement pension becomes payable` month `month in which the retirement pension becomes payable`
    AND `s 13(1.2)(c) — the month is not after the month in which the person reaches seventy years of age` month `date of birth`

§§ `Section 13(1) -- the proportion of the year`

-- src:361 | Amount of contributory self-employed earnings
-- src:362 | 13 (1) The amount of the contributory self-employed earnings of a person for a year is the amount of the self-employed earnings except that,
-- src:363 | (a) for a year in which the person reaches eighteen or seventy years of age, in which their contributory period ends under this Act or under a provincial pension plan by reason of disability or in which a disability pension ceases to be payable to them under this Act or under a provincial pension plan, the amount of the contributory self-employed earnings is equal to that proportion of the amount of the self-employed earnings that the number of months in the year
-- src:364 | (i) after
-- src:365 | (A) they reach eighteen years of age, or
-- src:366 | (B) the disability pension ceases to be payable, or
-- src:367 | (ii) before
-- src:368 | (A) they reach seventy years of age, or
-- src:369 | (B) the month following the month in which their contributory period ends under this Act or under a provincial pension plan by reason of disability,
-- src:370 | is of 12;
-- src:371 | (b) despite paragraph (a), for a year in which a retirement pension is payable to them under this Act or under a provincial pension plan and for which they make an election to exclude self-employed earnings, the amount of the contributory self-employed earnings is equal to that proportion of the amount of the self-employed earnings that the number of months in the year before the election is deemed to be made — minus the number of months that are excluded from the contributory period under this Act or under a provincial pension plan by reason of disability — is of 12;
-- src:372 | (c) despite paragraph (a), for a year in which a retirement pension is payable to them under this Act or under a provincial pension plan and for which they revoke an election to exclude self-employed earnings, the amount of the contributory self-employed earnings is equal to that proportion of the amount of the self-employed earnings that the number of months in the year after the election is deemed to be revoked — minus the number of months after they reach seventy years of age — is of 12;
-- src:373 | (d) despite paragraph (a), for a year in which an election referred to in subparagraph 12(1)(c)(ii) is made, the amount of the contributory self-employed earnings is equal to that proportion of the amount of the self-employed earnings that the number of months in the year before the election is made — minus the number of months that are excluded from the contributory period under this Act or under a provincial pension plan by reason of disability — is of 12; and
-- src:374 | (e) despite paragraph (a), for a year in which an election referred to in subparagraph 12(1)(c)(ii) is revoked, the amount of the contributory self-employed earnings is equal to that proportion of the amount of the self-employed earnings that the number of months in the year after the election is revoked — minus the number of months after they reach seventy years of age — is of 12.
-- Each of paragraphs (a) to (e) gives the contributory self-employed earnings as a proportion of the self-employed earnings,
-- the number of months of the year being of 12. A NUMBER of months below zero is no months (NOTES.md, fork register).
-- NOTHING: the paragraph does not apply to the facts.

@ref Act s 13(1)(a) (src:363-370)
GIVEN facts IS A `cp1 Facts about a person for a year`
      `the self-employed earnings of the person for the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 13(1)(a) — the contributory self-employed earnings for a year in which the person reaches eighteen or seventy, the contributory period ends or the disability pension ceases` facts `the self-employed earnings of the person for the year` MEANS
    -- Section 13 does not count the person's death (the paragraph does not list it).
    IF `a paragraph (a) event occurs in the year` facts FALSE
    THEN JUST (`the self-employed earnings of the person for the year` TIMES (`the number of months counted under paragraph (a)` facts FALSE) DIVIDED BY 12)
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref Act s 13(1)(b) (src:371)
GIVEN facts IS A `cp1 Facts about a person for a year`
      `the self-employed earnings of the person for the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 13(1)(b) — the contributory self-employed earnings for a year in which a retirement pension is payable and an election to exclude self-employed earnings is deemed made` facts `the self-employed earnings of the person for the year` MEANS
    CONSIDER facts's `month referred to in the election of the person under paragraph 13(1)(b)`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST election THEN
        IF DATE_YEAR election EQUALS facts's `the year at hand` AND `a retirement pension is payable to the person in the year` facts
        THEN JUST (`the self-employed earnings of the person for the year`
                   -- the months in the year before the election is deemed to be made, minus the months excluded by reason of disability
                   TIMES (max 0 (`the number of months of a year before a first day` (facts's `the year at hand`) (`s 13(1.1)(e) — the day on which the election is deemed to be made or revoked` election)
                                 MINUS `the number of months of the year excluded from the contributory period by reason of disability` facts))
                   DIVIDED BY 12)
        ELSE NOTHING

@ref Act s 13(1)(c) (src:372)
GIVEN facts IS A `cp1 Facts about a person for a year`
      `the self-employed earnings of the person for the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 13(1)(c) — the contributory self-employed earnings for a year in which a retirement pension is payable and an election to exclude self-employed earnings is deemed revoked` facts `the self-employed earnings of the person for the year` MEANS
    CONSIDER facts's `month referred to in the revocation by the person under paragraph 13(1)(c)`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST revocation THEN
        IF DATE_YEAR revocation EQUALS facts's `the year at hand` AND `a retirement pension is payable to the person in the year` facts
        THEN JUST (`the self-employed earnings of the person for the year`
                   -- the months in the year after the election is deemed to be revoked, minus the months after they reach seventy
                   TIMES (max 0 (`the number of months of a year from a first day` (facts's `the year at hand`) (`s 13(1.1)(e) — the day on which the election is deemed to be made or revoked` revocation)
                                 MINUS `the number of months of the year after the person reaches seventy years of age or dies, whichever is earlier` facts `paragraph 13(1)(c)` FALSE))
                   DIVIDED BY 12)
        ELSE NOTHING

@ref Act s 13(1)(d) (src:373)
GIVEN facts IS A `cp1 Facts about a person for a year`
      `the self-employed earnings of the person for the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 13(1)(d) — the contributory self-employed earnings for a year in which an election under subparagraph 12(1)(c)(ii) is made` facts `the self-employed earnings of the person for the year` MEANS
    CONSIDER facts's `date the person makes an election under subparagraph 12(1)(c)(ii)`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST made THEN
        IF DATE_YEAR made EQUALS facts's `the year at hand`
        THEN JUST (`the self-employed earnings of the person for the year`
                   -- the months in the year before the election is made (it has effect from the first day of the next month), minus the months excluded by reason of disability
                   TIMES (max 0 (`the number of months of a year before a first day` (facts's `the year at hand`) (`s 12(1.1)(b) — the first day on which the election has effect` made)
                                 MINUS `the number of months of the year excluded from the contributory period by reason of disability` facts))
                   DIVIDED BY 12)
        ELSE NOTHING

@ref Act s 13(1)(e) (src:374)
GIVEN facts IS A `cp1 Facts about a person for a year`
      `the self-employed earnings of the person for the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 13(1)(e) — the contributory self-employed earnings for a year in which an election under subparagraph 12(1)(c)(ii) is revoked` facts `the self-employed earnings of the person for the year` MEANS
    CONSIDER facts's `date the person revokes the election under subparagraph 12(1)(c)(ii)`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
    WHEN JUST revoked THEN
        IF DATE_YEAR revoked EQUALS facts's `the year at hand`
        THEN JUST (`the self-employed earnings of the person for the year`
                   -- the months in the year after the election is revoked (it ceases to have effect on the first day of the next month), minus the months after they reach seventy
                   TIMES (max 0 (`the number of months of a year from a first day` (facts's `the year at hand`) (`s 12(1.1)(c) — the first day on which the election ceases to have effect` revoked)
                                 MINUS `the number of months of the year after the person reaches seventy years of age or dies, whichever is earlier` facts `paragraph 13(1)(e)` FALSE))
                   DIVIDED BY 12)
        ELSE NOTHING

§§ `Section 13(2) and (4) -- excluded earnings, and earnings under a provincial plan`

-- src:388 | Excluded earnings
-- src:389 | (2) Subject to subsection (1), the contributory self-employed earnings of a person do not include earnings for
-- src:390 | (a) any period described in paragraph 12(1)(a), (b), (c) or (d); or
-- src:391 | (b) any year that
-- src:392 | (i) follows a year for which the person makes an election to exclude self-employed earnings, and
-- src:393 | (ii) is not a year for which they revoke the election.
-- (a) any period described in paragraph 12(1)(a), (b), (c) or (d): the month is one whose income subsection 12(1) leaves out.
@ref Act s 13(2)(a) (src:390)
GIVEN facts IS A `cp1 Facts about a person for a year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 13(2)(a) — the number of months of the year in a period described in paragraph 12(1)(a), (b), (c) or (d)` facts MEANS
    count (filter (GIVEN month YIELD `s 12(1) — income received on a date is not included in the contributory salary and wages` facts month)
                  (`the twelve months of a year` (facts's `the year at hand`)))

-- (b) any year that follows a year for which the person makes an election to exclude self-employed earnings and is not
-- a year for which they revoke the election. Reading taken (NOTES.md, fork register): the exclusion ends with the revocation.
@ref Act s 13(2)(b) (src:391-393)
GIVEN facts IS A `cp1 Facts about a person for a year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 13(2)(b) — the year follows a year for which the person makes an election to exclude self-employed earnings and is not a year for which they revoke it` facts MEANS
    CONSIDER facts's `month referred to in the election of the person under paragraph 13(1)(b)`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST made THEN
            DATE_YEAR made LESS THAN facts's `the year at hand`
        AND (CONSIDER facts's `month referred to in the revocation by the person under paragraph 13(1)(c)`
             WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
             WHEN JUST revoked THEN facts's `the year at hand` LESS THAN DATE_YEAR revoked)

-- The contributory self-employed earnings of a person for a year: paragraphs (b) to (e) apply despite (a); where none of
-- (a) to (e) applies, subsection (2) leaves out a year wholly within the periods of paragraph 12(1)(a) to (d), or following an
-- election; a year partly within those periods, where (1) does not apply, is not apportioned by the text.
@ref Act s 13(1) (src:361-374)
GIVEN facts IS A `cp1 Facts about a person for a year`
      `the self-employed earnings of the person for the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 13 — the contributory self-employed earnings of a person for a year` facts `the self-employed earnings of the person for the year` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- two election events in one year: the text bars two of one kind, and is silent on one of each
        IF `the election event in the year` facts EQUALS `more than one election event in the year` THEN NOTHING
        IF isJust `paragraph (b)` THEN `paragraph (b)`
        IF isJust `paragraph (c)` THEN `paragraph (c)`
        IF isJust `paragraph (d)` THEN `paragraph (d)`
        IF isJust `paragraph (e)` THEN `paragraph (e)`
        IF isJust `paragraph (a)` THEN `paragraph (a)`
        -- subsection (2)(b): a year after the election year, before its revocation
        IF `s 13(2)(b) — the year follows a year for which the person makes an election to exclude self-employed earnings and is not a year for which they revoke it` facts THEN JUST 0
        -- subsection (2)(a): the whole year within the periods of paragraph 12(1)(a) to (d)
        IF `months left out` EQUALS 12 THEN JUST 0
        -- no month of the year is left out
        IF `months left out` EQUALS 0 THEN JUST `the self-employed earnings of the person for the year`
        -- some months left out, and subsection (1) does not apportion the year: the text is silent
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `paragraph (a)` MEANS `s 13(1)(a) — the contributory self-employed earnings for a year in which the person reaches eighteen or seventy, the contributory period ends or the disability pension ceases` facts `the self-employed earnings of the person for the year`
        `paragraph (b)` MEANS `s 13(1)(b) — the contributory self-employed earnings for a year in which a retirement pension is payable and an election to exclude self-employed earnings is deemed made` facts `the self-employed earnings of the person for the year`
        `paragraph (c)` MEANS `s 13(1)(c) — the contributory self-employed earnings for a year in which a retirement pension is payable and an election to exclude self-employed earnings is deemed revoked` facts `the self-employed earnings of the person for the year`
        `paragraph (d)` MEANS `s 13(1)(d) — the contributory self-employed earnings for a year in which an election under subparagraph 12(1)(c)(ii) is made` facts `the self-employed earnings of the person for the year`
        `paragraph (e)` MEANS `s 13(1)(e) — the contributory self-employed earnings for a year in which an election under subparagraph 12(1)(c)(ii) is revoked` facts `the self-employed earnings of the person for the year`
        `months left out` MEANS `s 13(2)(a) — the number of months of the year in a period described in paragraph 12(1)(a), (b), (c) or (d)` facts

-- src:429 | Self-employed earnings where resident in province
-- src:430 | (4) A reference in this Act to the contributory self-employed earnings of a person for a year shall, in relation to any self-employed earnings of a person who was resident on the last day of the year in a province providing a comprehensive pension plan, be construed as a reference to his self-employed earnings for the year as such earnings are required to be computed under the provincial pension plan of that province.
@ref Act s 13(4) (src:429-430)
GIVEN `the person was resident on the last day of the year in a province providing a comprehensive pension plan` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the self-employed earnings for the year as the provincial pension plan requires them to be computed` IS A NUMBER
      `the contributory self-employed earnings as this Act works them out` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 13(4) — the contributory self-employed earnings of a person resident in a province providing a comprehensive pension plan` `the person was resident on the last day of the year in a province providing a comprehensive pension plan` `the self-employed earnings for the year as the provincial pension plan requires them to be computed` `the contributory self-employed earnings as this Act works them out` MEANS
    IF `the person was resident on the last day of the year in a province providing a comprehensive pension plan`
    THEN `the self-employed earnings for the year as the provincial pension plan requires them to be computed`
    ELSE `the contributory self-employed earnings as this Act works them out`

§§ `Section 13(3) to (3.2) -- the election to include certain earnings`

-- src:394 | Election to include certain earnings — base contribution
-- src:395 | (3) Despite subsection (1), the amount of the contributory self-employed earnings of a person for a year for the purposes of subsection 10(1) shall, if the person or their representative makes an election in the prescribed form and manner within one year from June 15 in the following year — or, in the case of an employee to whom the Minister refunds an amount under section 38, from the day on which the Minister refunds the amount — include any amount by which
-- src:396 | (a) the lesser of
-- src:397 | (i) his contributory salary and wages for the year, and
-- src:398 | (ii) his maximum pensionable earnings for the year,
-- src:399 | exceeds
-- src:400 | (b) the aggregate of
-- src:401 | (i) the person’s salary and wages on which a base contribution has been made for the year and the amount, if any, that is determined in the prescribed manner to be the person’s salary and wages on which a base contribution has been made for the year by the person under a provincial pension plan, and
-- src:402 | (ii) the lesser of
-- src:403 | (A) the aggregate of all amounts deducted as prescribed on account of his basic exemption for the year by one or more employers pursuant to section 8 and all amounts deducted as prescribed by or under a provincial pension plan on account of any like exemption for the year by one or more employers pursuant to such a plan, and
-- src:404 | (B) his basic exemption for the year.
-- Time: "within one year from June 15 in the following year -- or, in the case of an employee to whom the Minister refunds an
-- amount under section 38, from the day on which the Minister refunds the amount". Reading taken (NOTES.md, fork register):
-- an election made on or before the end of that year is in time; the text sets no start.
@ref Act s 13(3) (src:394-395)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      `date the election is made` IS A DATE
      `day on which the Minister refunds an amount under section 38 to the employee` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 13(3) — the election is made in time` year `date the election is made` `day on which the Minister refunds an amount under section 38 to the employee` MEANS
    `date the election is made` AT MOST `the date a time limit ends` `day the year is counted from` (`a number of years` WITH `number of years` IS 1)
    WHERE
        `day the year is counted from` MEANS
            CONSIDER `day on which the Minister refunds an amount under section 38 to the employee`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN YMD (year PLUS 1) 6 15
            WHEN JUST refunded THEN refunded

@ref Act s 13(3) (src:394-404)
GIVEN `the person's contributory salary and wages for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the person's maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the person's salary and wages on which a base contribution has been made for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount, if any, determined in the prescribed manner to be the person's salary and wages on which a base contribution has been made for the year by the person under a provincial pension plan` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the aggregate of all amounts deducted as prescribed on account of the person's basic exemption for the year by one or more employers pursuant to section 8 and by or under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER
      `the person's basic exemption for the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 13(3) — the amount included in the contributory self-employed earnings for the purposes of subsection 10(1)`
        `the person's contributory salary and wages for the year`
        `the person's maximum pensionable earnings for the year`
        `the person's salary and wages on which a base contribution has been made for the year`
        `the amount, if any, determined in the prescribed manner to be the person's salary and wages on which a base contribution has been made for the year by the person under a provincial pension plan`
        `the aggregate of all amounts deducted as prescribed on account of the person's basic exemption for the year by one or more employers pursuant to section 8 and by or under a provincial pension plan`
        `the person's basic exemption for the year`
    MEANS
        `the amount by which one amount exceeds another` `paragraph (a)` `paragraph (b)`
    WHERE
        -- (a) the lesser of (i) the contributory salary and wages and (ii) the maximum pensionable earnings
        `paragraph (a)` MEANS min `the person's contributory salary and wages for the year` `the person's maximum pensionable earnings for the year`
        -- (b) the aggregate of (i) the salary and wages already contributed on (with the provincial amount, if any) and (ii) the lesser of (A) the exemption already deducted and (B) the basic exemption
        `paragraph (b)` MEANS
            (`the person's salary and wages on which a base contribution has been made for the year`
             PLUS fromMaybe 0 `the amount, if any, determined in the prescribed manner to be the person's salary and wages on which a base contribution has been made for the year by the person under a provincial pension plan`)
            PLUS (min `the aggregate of all amounts deducted as prescribed on account of the person's basic exemption for the year by one or more employers pursuant to section 8 and by or under a provincial pension plan` `the person's basic exemption for the year`)

-- src:405 | Earnings — first additional contribution
-- src:406 | (3.1) For 2019 and each subsequent year, if a person or their representative makes an election under subsection (3), the amount of the contributory self-employed earnings of the person for a year for the purposes of subsection 10(1.1) shall include any amount by which
-- src:407 | (a) the lesser of
-- src:408 | (i) the person’s contributory salary and wages for the year, and
-- src:409 | (ii) the person’s maximum pensionable earnings for the year,
-- src:410 | exceeds
-- src:411 | (b) the aggregate of
-- src:412 | (i) the person’s salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year and the amount, if any, that is determined in the prescribed manner to be the person’s salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year by the person under a provincial pension plan, and
-- src:413 | (ii) the lesser of
-- src:414 | (A) the aggregate of all amounts deducted as prescribed on account of the person’s basic exemption for the year by one or more employers under section 8 and all amounts deducted as prescribed by or under a provincial pension plan on account of any like exemption for the year by one or more employers under that plan, and
-- src:415 | (B) the person’s basic exemption for the year.
@ref Act s 13(3.1) (src:405-415)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      `the person or their representative makes an election under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person's contributory salary and wages for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the person's maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the person's salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount, if any, determined in the prescribed manner to be the person's salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year by the person under a provincial pension plan` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the aggregate of all amounts deducted as prescribed on account of the person's basic exemption for the year by one or more employers under section 8 and by or under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER
      `the person's basic exemption for the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 13(3.1) — the amount included in the contributory self-employed earnings for the purposes of subsection 10(1.1)`
        year
        `the person or their representative makes an election under subsection (3)`
        `the person's contributory salary and wages for the year`
        `the person's maximum pensionable earnings for the year`
        `the person's salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year`
        `the amount, if any, determined in the prescribed manner to be the person's salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year by the person under a provincial pension plan`
        `the aggregate of all amounts deducted as prescribed on account of the person's basic exemption for the year by one or more employers under section 8 and by or under a provincial pension plan`
        `the person's basic exemption for the year`
    MEANS
        -- "For 2019 and each subsequent year, if a person or their representative makes an election under subsection (3)"
        IF year AT LEAST 2019 AND `the person or their representative makes an election under subsection (3)`
        THEN JUST (`the amount by which one amount exceeds another` `paragraph (a)` `paragraph (b)`)
        ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        `paragraph (a)` MEANS min `the person's contributory salary and wages for the year` `the person's maximum pensionable earnings for the year`
        `paragraph (b)` MEANS
            (`the person's salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year`
             PLUS fromMaybe 0 `the amount, if any, determined in the prescribed manner to be the person's salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year by the person under a provincial pension plan`)
            PLUS (min `the aggregate of all amounts deducted as prescribed on account of the person's basic exemption for the year by one or more employers under section 8 and by or under a provincial pension plan` `the person's basic exemption for the year`)

-- src:416 | Earnings — second additional contribution
-- src:417 | (3.2) For 2024 and each subsequent year, if a person or their representative makes an election under subsection (3), the amount of the contributory self-employed earnings of the person for a year for the purposes of subsection 10(1.2) shall include any amount by which
-- src:418 | (a) the lesser of
-- src:419 | (i) the person’s contributory salary and wages for the year, and
-- src:420 | (ii) the person’s additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year,
-- src:421 | exceeds
-- src:422 | (b) the aggregate of
-- src:423 | (i) the person’s salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year and the person’s salary and wages on which a second additional contribution has been made for the year,
-- src:424 | (i.1) the amount, if any, that is determined in the prescribed manner to be the person’s salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year by the person under a provincial pension plan and the person’s salary and wages on which a second additional contribution has been made for the year by the person under a provincial pension plan,
-- src:425 | (ii) the lesser of
-- src:426 | (A) the aggregate of all amounts deducted as prescribed on account of the person’s basic exemption for the year by one or more employers under section 8 and all amounts deducted as prescribed by or under a provincial pension plan on account of any like exemption for the year by one or more employers under that plan, and
-- src:427 | (B) the person’s basic exemption for the year, and
-- src:428 | (iii) the amount calculated under subsection (3) or (3.1), if any.
@ref Act s 13(3.2) (src:416-428)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      `the person or their representative makes an election under subsection (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person's contributory salary and wages for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the person's additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the person's salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the person's salary and wages on which a second additional contribution has been made for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount, if any, determined in the prescribed manner to be the person's salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year by the person under a provincial pension plan` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the amount, if any, determined in the prescribed manner to be the person's salary and wages on which a second additional contribution has been made for the year by the person under a provincial pension plan` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the aggregate of all amounts deducted as prescribed on account of the person's basic exemption for the year by one or more employers under section 8 and by or under a provincial pension plan` IS A NUMBER
      `the person's basic exemption for the year` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount, if any, calculated under subsection (3) or (3.1)` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 13(3.2) — the amount included in the contributory self-employed earnings for the purposes of subsection 10(1.2)`
        year
        `the person or their representative makes an election under subsection (3)`
        `the person's contributory salary and wages for the year`
        `the person's additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year`
        `the person's salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year`
        `the person's salary and wages on which a second additional contribution has been made for the year`
        `the amount, if any, determined in the prescribed manner to be the person's salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year by the person under a provincial pension plan`
        `the amount, if any, determined in the prescribed manner to be the person's salary and wages on which a second additional contribution has been made for the year by the person under a provincial pension plan`
        `the aggregate of all amounts deducted as prescribed on account of the person's basic exemption for the year by one or more employers under section 8 and by or under a provincial pension plan`
        `the person's basic exemption for the year`
        `the amount, if any, calculated under subsection (3) or (3.1)`
    MEANS
        -- "For 2024 and each subsequent year, if a person or their representative makes an election under subsection (3)"
        IF year AT LEAST 2024 AND `the person or their representative makes an election under subsection (3)`
        THEN JUST (`the amount by which one amount exceeds another` `paragraph (a)` `paragraph (b)`)
        ELSE NOTHING
    WHERE
        -- (a) the lesser of (i) the contributory salary and wages and (ii) the additional maximum pensionable earnings
        `paragraph (a)` MEANS min `the person's contributory salary and wages for the year` `the person's additional maximum pensionable earnings for the year`
        -- (b) the aggregate of (i) the first and second additional salary and wages, (i.1) the provincial amounts, (ii) the lesser of (A) and (B), and (iii) the amount under (3) or (3.1), if any
        `paragraph (b)` MEANS
            (`the person's salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year` PLUS `the person's salary and wages on which a second additional contribution has been made for the year`)
            PLUS (fromMaybe 0 `the amount, if any, determined in the prescribed manner to be the person's salary and wages on which a first additional contribution has been made for the year by the person under a provincial pension plan`
                  PLUS fromMaybe 0 `the amount, if any, determined in the prescribed manner to be the person's salary and wages on which a second additional contribution has been made for the year by the person under a provincial pension plan`)
            PLUS (min `the aggregate of all amounts deducted as prescribed on account of the person's basic exemption for the year by one or more employers under section 8 and by or under a provincial pension plan` `the person's basic exemption for the year`)
            PLUS fromMaybe 0 `the amount, if any, calculated under subsection (3) or (3.1)`
